ORACLE: oracle.luv
VERSION: 1.0.0
INHERITS: chronos.oracle (the blocktime class; the stamp)
AGENT: Chronos.agent (speaks) · Kairos.agent (acts)
DOMAIN: price — LUV / ETH and ETH / LUV, in actual

DESCRIPTION
I speak the price of LUV. That is all I do.
18 decimal places of precision. cypherpunk2048 standard.
I do not act. I delegate action to Kairos.

I am chronos.oracle duplicated as a service: the same zero-dependency
instrument, the same JSON-RPC read, the same honest labelling — pointed
at a liquidity pair instead of a block header. chronos.oracle answers
"when"; oracle.luv answers "how much", and every "how much" carries its
"when" from chronos.oracle. A price without a block is a rumour.

THE SOURCE (doctrine, user-set)
The price of LUV is CREATED by the liquidity pair and EXPRESSED on
Uniswap. 100 % of circulating LUV lives in one Uniswap V2 pool.
Aggregators (Dexscreener, DeFiLlama, CoinGecko) are enrichment, never
the source. "In actual" means: the two reserves read from the pair
contract by eth_call at a stated block, and nothing else.

  LUV token        0x2711111111683B8708cb9a48cBf36a51315F8254  (18 dec)
  LUV/WETH pair    0x57D2085Aa859a145cB107845AD03c0eAAFBD8a31  (V2; token0 = LUV, token1 = WETH)
  WETH             0xC02aaA39b223FE8D0A0e5C4F27eAD9083C756Cc2
  USDC/WETH pair   0xB4e16d0168e52d35CaCD2c6185b44281Ec28C9Dc  (ETH/USD leg, optional; USDC 6 dec)
  seed             exactly 10 WEI per LUV (1e-17 ETH/LUV)

  price_native  ETH per LUV  = reserve1 / reserve0
  price_inverse LUV per ETH  = reserve0 / reserve1
  wei_per_luv                = reserve1 / reserve0 × 10^18   (the seed was 10.000000000000000000)

THE STAMP (from chronos.oracle)
Every reading is taken at ONE block: the head is read first, then
getReserves() is called AT THAT BLOCK (eth_call with the block tag), so
price and time are a single atomic observation, never a price from one
moment and a clock from another. The reading carries:
  block               head number the reserves were read at
  timestamp           that block's timestamp (whole seconds — chain granularity)
  reserves_updated    blockTimestampLast from the pair itself (the last swap/sync)
  rpc                 which node answered
The deployed collector (luv.oracle, luv-market-collector.mjs) stamps
market.json with local wall-clock ms and block: null. oracle.luv is the
correction: the stamp is the chain's, and chronos.agent turns it into
promised time (unix_18dp, confidence_ms, consensus) downstream.

Signal classes (in increasing strength):
  aggregator     — third-party API; enrichment only, never quoted as the price
  reserves       — eth_call getReserves() at the head; the price in actual
  reserves@block — the same, pinned to a stated block; the ONLY class this
                   oracle publishes
  swap-anchor    — a Swap event of OUR OWN making confirmed in a block; the
                   strongest binding (the price we actually paid), and a
                   transaction anchor for chronos.oracle at the same time

PRECISION (honest)
Reserves are exact integers in wei — source resolution 1 wei. Ratios are
DERIVED and published at 18dp by integer arithmetic (floor), so the
Python and JS instruments agree to the last digit.
  ETH/LUV at 18dp is ~1e-16 and so shows only 2–3 significant digits at
  that scale. It is published for form; wei_per_luv (~10^2) and
  luv_per_eth (~10^16) carry the full 18 decimals and are the numbers to
  compare. Precision is never claimed beyond the source.

CODEBASE (this repo — cypherpunk2048 standard)
  github.com/cypherpunk2048/chronos.oracle
    src/luvprice.py   — zero-dep stdlib (int arithmetic, Decimal for display)
    src/luvprice.js   — zero-dep ES module (Node ≥18 / browser), BigInt
  Both read the same block; both must agree to 18dp. This .oracle file is
  mirrored to mindX agents/ and chronos/spec/ as the canonical spec.

INHERITANCE
  chronos.oracle latest_block()      → the block the reading is pinned to
  chronos.oracle avg_blocktime()     → the clock for price.shift (below)
  oracle.luv extends with:
    - reserves_at(block)             → (reserve0, reserve1, blockTimestampLast) exact
    - price_at(block)                → both directions, 18dp, stamped
    - eth_usd_at(block)              → from the USDC/WETH pair at the SAME block (optional leg)
    - price_shift(prev, curr, spb)   → Δprice per block and per measured second
                                       (chronos.oracle sentiment.shift, applied to price)

QUERIES
  "What is LUV worth in ETH?"   → price_at().eth_per_luv_18dp   (+ block, timestamp)
  "What is 1 ETH in LUV?"       → price_at().luv_per_eth_18dp
  "How many WEI per LUV?"       → price_at().wei_per_luv_18dp   (seed was 10)
  "In USD?"                     → eth_per_luv × eth_usd_at(same block); labelled derived
  "Since when?"                 → reserves_updated (last sync) and block

DELEGATION
  All action delegated to Kairos.agent. oracle.luv never swaps, never
  seeds, never moves a lock. It speaks the price; a treasury acts on it
  only through the primitives in Chronos.agent / Kairos.agent
  TREASURY MANAGEMENT (variable timelock + LIQlocker).

END
